  "model_card": {
    "summary": "Final dense-budget and top-1/top-2 four-expert TinyLM variants, with and without load-balancing loss.",
    "scope": "分別以完整模型total與每token active參數代理匹配Dense，width取最近4倍數。相同資料/token/更新預算；active參數不是精確FLOPs，路由與索引成本另看實測時間。",
    "limitations": [
      "Single seed, short training and small fixed datasets do not establish universal architecture or precision superiority.",
      "Active parameter count is a proxy rather than measured FLOPs; routing/indexing overhead and dropless Python dispatch may prevent speedups.",
      "All seven models start from fresh random initialization; only matching-shape initial tables are copied. No modern or real_text checkpoint is loaded. Dense width changes also change representation capacity and table shapes.",
      "Dense widths are the nearest multiple of four to the stated parameter target. dense_total has 329888 parameters versus the MoE target 340608, about 3.15% fewer; the three budget comparisons are approximate rather than exact parameter or FLOP matches.",
      "top2_aux0.01.pt is the predeclared downstream teacher, not the best-quality variant: test NLL is 2.3017035253733837 versus dense_total 2.249425529199298. The sampled continuations are repetitive; this short run does not establish coherent general story generation.",
      "This implementation retains the top-1 softmax gate rather than renormalizing it to one. Its measured task-loss router gradients are nonzero; the auxiliary gradient is reported separately. Routing balance does not establish human-interpretable expert specialization."
    ],
